      "title": "[Wikipedia  - Recent changes [en]] Cider",
      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Midwest_hard_cider.jpg/1280px-Midwest_hard_cider.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\"/>\n<p><span class=\"autocomment\">Variations and related drinks: </span> Moved to \"related drinks\" or variations</p>\n<table style=\"background-color:#fff;color:#202122;\">\n<tr class=\"diff-title\" lang=\"en\">\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"background-color:#fff;color:#202122;text-align:center;\">← Previous revision</td>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"background-color:#fff;color:#202122;text-align:center;\">Revision as of 04:02, 7 October 2026</td>\n</tr><tr>\n<td class=\"diff-lineno\" colspan=\"2\">Line 216:</td>\n<td class=\"diff-lineno\" colspan=\"2\">Line 216:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"diff-marker\"></td>\n<td style=\"background-color:#f8f9fa;color:#202122;font-size:88%;border-style:solid;border-width:1px 1px 1px 4px;border-radius:0.33em;border-color:#eaecf0;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br/></td>\n<td class=\"diff-marker\"></td>\n<td style=\"background-color:#f8f9fa;color:#202122;font-size:88%;border-style:solid;border-width:1px 1px 1px 4px;border-radius:0.33em;border-color:#eaecf0;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br/></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"diff-marker\"></td>\n<td style=\"background-color:#f8f9fa;color:#202122;font-size:88%;border-style:solid;border-width:1px 1px 1px 4px;border-radius:0.33em;border-color:#eaecf0;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><div>== Variations and related drinks ==</div></td>\n<td class=\"diff-marker\"></td>\n<td style=\"background-color:#f8f9fa;color:#202122;font-size:88%;border-style:solid;border-width:1px 1px 1px 4px;border-radius:0.33em;border-color:#eaecf0;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><div>== Variations and related drinks ==</div></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"diff-empty diff-side-deleted\" colspan=\"2\"></td>\n<td class=\"diff-marker\"></td>\n<td style=\"color:#202122;font-size:88%;border-style:solid;border-width:1px 1px 1px 4px;border-radius:0.33em;border-color:#a3d3ff;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br/></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"diff-empty diff-side-deleted\" colspan=\"2\"></td>\n<td class=\"diff-marker\"></td>\n<td style=\"color:#202122;font-size:88%;border-style:solid;border-width:1px 1px 1px 4px;border-radius:0.33em;border-color:#a3d3ff;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><div>In addition to the UK and its former colonies, cider is popular in France (particularly [[Normandy]] and [[Brittany]]), Portugal (mainly in [[Entre-Douro-e-Minho Province|Minho]] and [[Madeira]]), northern Italy (specifically [[Friuli]]), and northern Spain (specifically [[Asturias]], [[Basque Country (greater region)|Basque Country]]). Due to fermentation, ciders can be thought of as a [[fruit wine]] made from apples, though the exact definitions of either beverage can vary by culture. Germany also has its own types of cider, with [[Rhineland-Palatinate]] and [[Hesse]] producing a particularly tart version known as [[Apfelwein]].</div></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"diff-marker\"></td>\n<td style=\"background-color:#f8f9fa;color:#202122;font-size:88%;border-style:solid;border-width:1px 1px 1px 4px;border-radius:0.33em;border-color:#eaecf0;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br/></td>\n<td class=\"diff-marker\"></td>\n<td style=\"background-color:#f8f9fa;color:#202122;font-size:88%;border-style:solid;border-width:1px 1px 1px 4px;border-radius:0.33em;border-color:#eaecf0;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><br/></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"diff-marker\"></td>\n<td style=\"background-color:#f8f9fa;color:#202122;font-size:88%;border-style:solid;border-width:1px 1px 1px 4px;border-radius:0.33em;border-color:#eaecf0;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><div>[[Calvados (brandy)|Calvados]] and [[Applejack (beverage)|applejack]] are strong liquors distilled from cider. They differ in their geographical origin and their method of distillation.&lt;ref&gt;{{Cite web |title=Applejack vs Calvados (Here's the difference!) – ExpertBrewing.com |url=https://expertbrewing.com/applejack-calvados-differences/ |access-date=14 June 2023 |website=expertbrewing.com}}&lt;/ref&gt;</div></td>\n<td class=\"diff-marker\"></td>\n<td style=\"background-color:#f8f9fa;color:#202122;font-size:88%;border-style:solid;border-width:1px 1px 1px 4px;border-radius:0.33em;border-color:#eaecf0;vertical-align:top;white-space:pre-wrap;\"><div>[[Calvados (brandy)|Calvados]] and [[Applejack (beverage)|applejack]] are strong liquors distilled from cider. They differ in their geographical origin and their method of distillation.&lt;ref&gt;{{Cite web |title=Applejack vs Calvados (Here's the difference!) – ExpertBrewing.com |url=https://expertbrewing.com/applejack-calvados-differences/ |access-date=14 June 2023 |website=expertbrewing.com}}&lt;/ref&gt;</div></td>\n</tr>\n</table>",
